.TH CISV 1 "May 2026" "cisv-cli 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cisv \- high-performance CSV parser and writer CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cisv
[\fBCOMMAND\fR] [\fBOPTIONS\fR] [\fBFILE\fR]
.br
.B cisv
\fBwrite\fR [\fBOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B cisv
\fBmerge rows\fR \fIFILE...\fR \fB--dedup-key\fR \fICOL\fR \fB--exclude-keys\fR \fIFILE:COL\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcisv\fR is a high-performance CSV command-line tool backed by \fBcisv-core\fR.
It supports parsing, row counting, column selection, head/tail output, native
row deduplication/exclusion/merge operations, benchmarking, and CSV generation
through the \fBwrite\fR subcommand.
.SH INPUT MODEL
.TP
.B File path
Default input mode. Provide a CSV file path as the last argument.
.TP
.B "-"
Use \fB-\fR to read CSV from stdin explicitly.
.TP
.B Piped stdin
If stdin is piped and no input file is provided, \fBcisv\fR reads stdin automatically.
.SH OUTPUT MODEL
.TP
.B CSV (default)
Rows are written as CSV to stdout (or \fB--output\fR file).
.TP
.B JSON (\fB--json\fR)
Outputs a JSON array. Header row is used as object keys unless \fB--no-header\fR.
.TP
.B JSONL (\fB--jsonl\fR)
Outputs one JSON object/array per line for streaming pipelines.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B parse
Parse a CSV file (default command when no command is provided).
.TP
.B write
Generate CSV output and benchmark writer throughput.
.TP
.B cat rows
Concatenate multiple CSV files by rows while preserving one header.
.TP
.B dedup
Deduplicate rows by one or more key columns.
.TP
.B filter exclude
Keep source rows whose key is not present in another CSV file.
.TP
.B merge rows
Concatenate sources, exclude deleted keys, then deduplicate in input order.
.SH PARSE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-delimiter \fIDELIM\fR
Set field delimiter (default: \fB,\fR).
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quote \fICHAR\fR
Set quote character (default: \fB"\fR).
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-escape \fICHAR\fR
Set escape character.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-comment \fICHAR\fR
Set comment character.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-trim
Trim whitespace from fields.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-relaxed
Enable relaxed parsing.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-empty
Skip empty lines.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-errors
Skip lines with parse errors.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Stop on first parse error (default behavior).
.TP
.B \-\-no-header
Skip first row in output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non-data stderr logs.
.TP
.B \-\-max-row \fISIZE\fR
Set max row size in bytes.
.TP
.B \-\-from-line \fIN\fR
Start from line \fIN\fR (1-based).
.TP
.B \-\-to-line \fIN\fR
Stop at line \fIN\fR.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-select \fICOLS\fR
Select comma-separated column indices.
.TP
.B \-\-select-name \fINAMES\fR
Select comma-separated column names from the header row.
.TP
.B \-\-where \fIEXPR\fR
Filter rows with expressions like \fBcol==value\fR, \fBcol>100\fR, or \fBcol~text\fR.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-count
Print row count only.
.TP
.B \-\-head \fIN\fR
Print first \fIN\fR rows.
.TP
.B \-\-tail \fIN\fR
Print last \fIN\fR rows.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Write output to file instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output JSON array format.
.TP
.B \-\-jsonl
Output JSON Lines format.
.TP
.B \-\-parallel
Use multi-threaded parsing.
.TP
.B \-\-threads \fIN\fR
Set worker thread count for parallel mode. Also enables \fB--parallel\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-max-procs \fIN\fR
Cap CISV worker threads/cores for automatic parallel work. Overrides \fBCISV_MAX_PROCS\fR and \fBGOMAXPROCS\fR for this process.
.TP
.B \-\-max-memory \fISIZE\fR
Set the CISV parser memory budget for this process. Accepts byte values and K/KB/KiB, M/MB/MiB, G/GB/GiB, or T/TB/TiB suffixes. Overrides \fBCISV_MAX_MEMORY\fR and \fBGOMEMLIMIT\fR for this process.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-benchmark
Run parser benchmark mode.
.SH ROW OPERATION OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-key \fICOL\fR
Key column name for \fBdedup\fR or \fBfilter exclude\fR. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-dedup-key \fICOL\fR
Key column name for \fBmerge rows\fR. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-key-index \fIN\fR
Zero-based key index for headerless input.
.TP
.B \-\-keep first|last
Dedup policy. Default is \fBfirst\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keys-file \fIFILE\fR
CSV file containing exclusion keys for \fBfilter exclude\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keys-file-key \fICOL\fR
Key column name in \fB--keys-file\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-keys \fIFILE:COL\fR
CSV file and key column for \fBmerge rows\fR exclusion.
.TP
.B \-\-stats-json \fIFILE\fR
Write machine-readable counters and timings.
.TP
.B \-\-memory-limit \fISIZE\fR
Soft memory budget for row operations.
.TP
.B \-\-external
Use partitioned disk-backed key processing. The current external mode supports
\fB--keep first\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-tmp-dir \fIDIR\fR
Temporary directory for external mode.
.TP
.B \-\-drop-empty-key
Skip rows whose full key is empty.
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-header-mismatch
Continue when later input headers differ, while counting mismatches.
.SH WHERE EXPRESSIONS
.TP
.B Equality / inequality
\fBcol==value\fR, \fBcol!=value\fR
.TP
.B Numeric comparison
\fBcol>100\fR, \fBcol>=100\fR, \fBcol<100\fR, \fBcol<=100\fR
.TP
.B Contains
\fBcol~text\fR
.TP
.B Column reference
\fBcol\fR can be a zero-based index (\fB0\fR, \fB1\fR, ...) or a header name
when a header row is present.
.SH WRITE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-generate \fIN\fR
Generate \fIN\fR rows of synthetic CSV data.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Write output to file.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-delimiter \fICHAR\fR
Set output delimiter.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quote \fICHAR\fR
Set output quote character.
.TP
.B \-Q, \-\-always-quote
Always quote output fields.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-crlf
Use CRLF line endings.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-null \fISTRING\fR
Text to output for NULL fields.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-columns \fILIST\fR
Column names for generation mode.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-benchmark
Run writer benchmark mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Parse and print:
.B cisv data.csv
.TP
Count rows only:
.B cisv \-c data.csv
.TP
Select columns 0 and 2:
.B cisv \-s 0,2 data.csv
.TP
Parse stdin stream:
.B cat data.csv | cisv -
.TP
Parse TSV and emit JSONL:
.B cisv -d $'\\t' --jsonl data.tsv
.TP
Select by header name:
.B cisv --select-name id,name data.csv
.TP
Filter rows:
.B cisv --where 'status==ok' data.csv
.TP
Parse with four worker threads:
.B cisv --parallel --threads 4 data.csv
.TP
Filter by numeric threshold:
.B cisv --where 'latency_ms>100' data.csv
.TP
Filter substring match:
.B cisv --where 'email~@example.com' data.csv
.TP
JSON output:
.B cisv --json data.csv
.TP
Pipeline from stdin to file:
.B cat data.csv | cisv --select-name id,name - > reduced.csv
.TP
Merge newest-first source files, exclude deleted IDs, and write stats:
.B cisv merge rows newest.csv middle.csv oldest.csv --dedup-key Id --exclude-keys deleted.csv:Id -o merged.csv --stats-json merged.stats.json
.TP
Deduplicate by last row:
.B cisv dedup data.csv --key Id --keep last
.TP
Filter rows by delete-key file:
.B cisv filter exclude data.csv --key Id --keys-file deleted.csv --keys-file-key Id
.TP
Generate one million rows:
.B cisv write \-g 1000000 \-o out.csv
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CISV_STATS
If set, print parser statistics to stderr after execution.
.TP
.B CISV_MAX_PROCS
Maximum CISV worker threads/cores. Takes precedence over \fBGOMAXPROCS\fR.
.TP
.B GOMAXPROCS
Go-compatible alias for the CISV worker thread/core cap when \fBCISV_MAX_PROCS\fR is unset.
.TP
.B CISV_MAX_MEMORY
Process-local CISV parser memory budget. Takes precedence over \fBGOMEMLIMIT\fR.
.TP
.B GOMEMLIMIT
Go-compatible alias for the CISV parser memory budget when \fBCISV_MAX_MEMORY\fR is unset.
.TP
.B CISV_MAX_ROW_SIZE
Default maximum logical row size when \fB--max-row\fR or API config leaves it unset.
.TP
.B CISV_PARALLEL_MIN_BYTES
Minimum file size before automatic parallel parsing can use more than one worker.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/bin/cisv
CLI binary.
.TP
.B /usr/share/man/man1/cisv.1
Manual page.
.SH NOTES
.TP
For best performance on very large files, avoid unnecessary format conversion
and prefer direct CSV output unless JSON/JSONL is required by downstream tools.
.TP
Use \fB--no-header\fR when processing CSV sources without header rows.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure.
.TP
.B 2
CLI usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
CSV parse error in strict mode.
.TP
.B 4
Missing key column.
.TP
.B 5
Header mismatch.
.TP
.B 6
I/O error.
.TP
.B 7
Memory limit cannot be honored.
.TP
.B 8
External/temp mode failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR awk (1),
.BR cut (1),
.BR sed (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/Sanix-Darker/cisv-cli
